---
import Book from "../layouts/Book.astro";
import ChapterOpener from "../components/ChapterOpener.astro";
import PipeBlock from "../components/PipeBlock.astro";
import data from "../data/skills.json";

const realCount = Object.entries(data.byCategory)
  .filter(([c]) => c !== "shortcut")
  .reduce((acc, [, list]) => acc + (list as any[]).length, 0);
const shortcutCount = (data.byCategory.shortcut as any[] | undefined)?.length ?? 0;
const total = realCount + shortcutCount;
---

<Book
  title="Install"
  chapter="install"
  description="Install Luna Agents — npm, Claude Code plugin, source. Includes troubleshooting for missing skills."
>
  <ChapterOpener
    num="04"
    word="Install"
    subtitle={`Three ways to get the binary. After install you have ${total} slash commands (${realCount} canonical, ${shortcutCount} shortcuts).`}
  />

  <section class="wrap">
    <h2>1. From npm.</h2>
    <p>The fastest path. Requires Node ≥ 18.</p>
    <PipeBlock
      code={'npm install -g luna-agents && luna-setup'}
      output={[
        'installed: luna-agents@latest',
        'detected: claude code at ~/.claude',
        `registered: ${total} slash commands`,
        'next: open Claude Code, try /luna-agents:cmds',
      ]}
    />

    <h2>2. As a Claude Code plugin.</h2>
    <p>
      After the npm install, the plugin is registered automatically. If
      you skipped <code>luna-setup</code>, or you want to install just
      the plugin without the CLI, do it inside Claude Code:
    </p>
    <PipeBlock
      caption="Inside Claude Code."
      code={'/plugin marketplace add lunaos-ai/luna-agents'}
      output={['marketplace added: luna-agents-marketplace (1 plugin)']}
    />
    <PipeBlock
      code={'/plugin install luna-agents@luna-agents-marketplace'}
      output={[
        'installing: luna-agents',
        `commands: ${total} (incl. shortcuts)`,
        `agents:   45`,
        'mcp:      luna-nexa-rag, luna-glm-vision, luna-vision-rag-client',
        'ok. run /reload-plugins to activate.',
      ]}
    />
    <p>
      Already installed something? Re-run <code>luna-setup</code> — it's
      idempotent.
    </p>

    <h2>3. From source.</h2>
    <p>For contributors and folks who want the head of main.</p>
    <PipeBlock
      code={'git clone https://github.com/lunaos-ai/luna-agents && cd luna-agents && npm install && ./setup.sh'}
      output={['cloned, installed, linked. luna binary now points at your working copy.']}
    />

    <h2>Verify.</h2>
    <PipeBlock
      code={'luna --version && luna pipe "persona generate >> ghost \\"hello\\""'}
      output={[
        'luna 2.0.1',
        'composed: 2 stages',
        '  [01] /persona generate',
        '  [02] /ghost "hello"',
        'ok.',
      ]}
    />
    <p>In Claude Code, type <code>/luna-agents:cmds</code> — you should see {total} commands.</p>

    <h2>Configure.</h2>
    <p>
      Most verbs work without keys. A few (image generation, voice, certain
      external APIs) need credentials. The runtime reads from your OS
      keychain first, then <code>.env</code>. Never paste keys into pipes.
    </p>
    <PipeBlock
      code={'luna config set openai_key && luna config set anthropic_key'}
      output={['stored in OS keychain. never written to disk in plaintext.']}
    />

    <h2 id="troubleshooting">Troubleshooting.</h2>

    <h3>I don't see all the skills / shortcuts after <code>npm install</code>.</h3>
    <p>
      Two causes, both fixable in 10 seconds:
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <strong>You're on an old version.</strong> The full skill set
        ships from <code>luna-agents@2.0.1</code> onward. Run{" "}
        <code>npm install -g luna-agents@latest</code> and then{" "}
        <code>luna-setup</code> again — it's idempotent.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>The plugin wasn't registered with Claude Code.</strong>
        Run <code>luna-setup</code>, or do it manually inside Claude Code
        with the two <code>/plugin</code> commands above. Then restart
        Claude Code (it loads plugin manifests at startup).
      </li>
    </ol>
    <PipeBlock
      caption="Force a clean reinstall."
      code={'npm uninstall -g luna-agents && npm install -g luna-agents@latest && luna-setup --force'}
      output={[
        'removed: 1 package',
        `installed: luna-agents@2.0.1 (${total} commands, 45 agents)`,
        'registered: claude code plugin (forced)',
        'next: restart claude code',
      ]}
    />

    <h3>The plugin is registered but commands don't autocomplete.</h3>
    <p>
      Claude Code caches the slash-command index per session. Restart
      it. If still empty, check{" "}
      <code>~/.claude/plugins/luna-agents/claude-plugin.json</code>
      exists and points to <code>commands/</code> — that's where the
      registrar reads from.
    </p>

    <h3>Where to read next.</h3>
    <ul class="next-list">
      <li><a href="/skills">Chapter 07 · Skills</a>, featured skills incl. <code>/ll-no-bluf</code>.</li>
      <li><a href="/lexicon">Chapter 01 · Lexicon</a>, every verb, with call signatures.</li>
      <li><a href="/grammar">Chapter 02 · Grammar</a>, the five operators in full.</li>
      <li><a href="/feedback">Chapter 08 · Feedback</a>, missing a skill? Tell us.</li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/lunaos-ai/luna-agents">Source</a>, the parser, runtime, and verb registry.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Book>

<style>
  section { padding: var(--t-6) 0 var(--t-12); }
  .next-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: var(--t-3) 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    max-width: var(--measure-wide);
  }
  .next-list li {
    margin: 0;
    padding: var(--t-2) 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }
  .next-list a { text-decoration-color: var(--saffron-deep); }
</style>
